WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.838 --> 00:00:02.545
The summer shutdown has begun.

2
00:00:03.286 --> 00:00:06.595
Line 3 has to stand in hall B in 3 weeks.

3
00:00:07.619 --> 00:00:08.629
The plan is ready.

4
00:00:09.335 --> 00:00:13.422
Now the point is to keep the project moving, every day of the shutdown.

5
00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.878
We follow this one project through the four topics of the module.

6
00:00:18.577 --> 00:00:21.155
The details come later, in the lessons.

7
00:00:22.485 --> 00:00:24.865
The first topic is Steering and reporting.

8
00:00:25.589 --> 00:00:27.203
How is the project really doing?

9
00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:31.027
The buyer reports that the switchboard will be late.

10
00:00:31.818 --> 00:00:34.501
It is a risk, but the team can still absorb it.

11
00:00:35.229 --> 00:00:36.773
So the status is amber.

12
00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:39.730
Tell the steering group at once.

13
00:00:40.442 --> 00:00:42.253
Bad news early is cheap.

14
00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:45.031
Bad news late is expensive.

15
00:00:46.026 --> 00:00:51.169
For steering and reporting we often use an A3 status report and a forecast.

16
00:00:52.513 --> 00:00:55.230
The second topic is Scope and change control.

17
00:00:55.937 --> 00:00:58.422
What is part of the project, and what is not?

18
00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.920
The team lead asks whether line 4 can come along too.

19
00:01:03.608 --> 00:01:06.011
Each request is small and reasonable.

20
00:01:06.763 --> 00:01:09.062
That is how the scope grows unnoticed.

21
00:01:09.825 --> 00:01:11.323
It is called scope creep.

22
00:01:12.369 --> 00:01:15.097
You do not say no, you show what it costs.

23
00:01:15.798 --> 00:01:17.400
Time, money and risk.

24
00:01:18.142 --> 00:01:21.335
It becomes a change request, and the sponsor chooses.

25
00:01:22.384 --> 00:01:27.376
For scope and change control we often use a change log and an impact analysis.

26
00:01:28.663 --> 00:01:30.997
The third topic is Team and meetings.

27
00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.050
How do you keep everyone on the same page?

28
00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.358
A project runs on three meetings.

29
00:01:38.111 --> 00:01:43.394
A short stand-up at the line, a weekly meeting and a steering group every few weeks.

30
00:01:44.412 --> 00:01:47.222
Every meeting ends in decisions and actions.

31
00:01:47.962 --> 00:01:50.586
With a name and a date, or nothing happens.

32
00:01:51.597 --> 00:01:55.486
For team and meetings we often use a decision note and minutes.

33
00:01:56.847 --> 00:01:59.448
The fourth topic is Issues and escalation.

34
00:02:00.162 --> 00:02:02.647
What is going wrong now, and who solves it?

35
00:02:03.686 --> 00:02:05.474
The late switchboard was a risk.

36
00:02:06.249 --> 00:02:08.710
Now that it is happening, it is an issue.

37
00:02:09.392 --> 00:02:12.109
A problem that is happening now and needs action.

38
00:02:13.102 --> 00:02:15.853
It goes into the issue log, with one owner.

39
00:02:16.582 --> 00:02:19.136
That is the buyer, a name and not the team.

40
00:02:20.134 --> 00:02:22.142
If that fails, you escalate.

41
00:02:22.894 --> 00:02:25.274
You put it with the sponsor, with a proposal.

42
00:02:26.265 --> 00:02:31.269
For issues and escalation we often use an escalation path and a decision log.

43
00:02:32.621 --> 00:02:33.747
It all connects.

44
00:02:34.439 --> 00:02:36.169
The team sees what is going on.

45
00:02:36.862 --> 00:02:41.460
The status reports it, and what the team cannot decide goes up to the sponsor.

46
00:02:42.508 --> 00:02:46.014
The sponsor chooses, line 4 comes after the shutdown.

47
00:02:46.751 --> 00:02:51.035
The decision is on the decision log, and everyone knows where they stand.

48
00:02:52.399 --> 00:02:54.082
This is the map of Projects.

49
00:02:54.825 --> 00:02:57.681
Run is the third station on the road of a project.

50
00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.491
Run has four topics, each with four levels.

51
00:03:02.468 --> 00:03:06.462
Start at the top, with Steering and reporting, at the first level.

52
00:03:07.498 --> 00:03:11.724
At the second level you prepare the steering group and control changes.

53
00:03:12.447 --> 00:03:15.442
You lead without authority and get decisions made.

54
00:03:16.488 --> 00:03:18.833
At the third level you steer with numbers,

55
00:03:18.972 --> 00:03:21.828
replan with reserves and escalate in tiers.

56
00:03:22.522 --> 00:03:26.760
The fourth level manages by exception and runs several workstreams.

57
00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:31.918
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
